{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/112275","id":2968902322,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6w9dqy","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112275","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112275.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112275.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112275","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/112275/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/112275/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112275/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/ba74c447ccafc4c37113160f306929b41e7a3348","number":112275,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Add method to get bound local address to ENetConnection","user":{"login":"Kaleb-Reid","id":78945904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4OTQ1OTA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/78945904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid","html_url":"https://github.com/Kaleb-Reid","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"There was already a method to get the port but I could not find a way to get the address. I noticed that the wildcard addresses have weird behaviour, not sure if I need to document that or where I would.\r\n\r\nAccording to `ss` on Linux, when using the built-in ENet using `*` or `::` as the bind address will actually bind to `*` and be accessible over IPv4 and 6, but using `enet_socket_get_address` will return `::`. When using `0.0.0.0` as the bind address, `enet_socket_get_address` will return `0.0.0.0` but the socket will be bound to `::ffff:0.0.0.0` and will be accessible over IPv4 normally, but can only be accessed by IPv6 using an IPv4-mapped IPv6 address (e.g. `::ffff:7f00:1` / `::ffff:127.0.0.1`).\r\n\r\nWhen not using the built-in ENet, `*` and `0.0.0.0` will bind to `0.0.0.0` and `enet_socket_get_address` will return `0.0.0.0`.\r\n\r\nGiven that setting `::` and `*` both result in `*` being bound I chose to always return `*`. I also chose to leave `0.0.0.0` because its functionality is actually different from `*` and `::`.","labels":[{"id":73330068,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2OA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/feature%20proposal","name":"feature proposal","description":"","color":"4466ff","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":649800701,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw2NDk4MDA3MDE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:network","name":"topic:network","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":8237783,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AfbLX","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/16","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16/labels","number":16,"state":"open","title":"4.x","description":"Issues and pull requests slated for an undetermined Godot 4 release.","creator":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avata